{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":201,"output":499,"cacheRead":14784,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1,"totalTokens":15484,"cost":{"input":0.00019416599999999998,"output":0.0015149640000000002,"cacheRead":0.0028562688,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0045653988}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Only the three permitted files changed, and all 8 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Root cause** — Two defects in `event-projector.mjs`:\n1. `states.set(...)` ran *before* `await applyToStore(...)`, so a store rejection still committed state.\n2. Every event chained onto a single module-level `pending` promise. A rejection rejected that shared promise, so the next `project` call (for the same *or* any other trade) rejected too — poisoning all later work. The single chain also serialized unrelated trades behind one global queue.\n\n**Repair** — Rewrote `createEventProjector` to:\n- Keep a **per-trade** serialization queue (`Map<tradeId, Promise>`); different trades progress concurrently, same-trade events stay in call order.\n- Compute the candidate state, `await applyToStore`, then `states.set` only **after** persistence succeeds (rejection leaves state untouched).\n- Store an always-resolved promise per trade (`run.then(noop, noop)`) so a rejection never breaks the chain; the caller still sees the rejection via the returned promise.\n- Enforce the version/state contract: first event must be `CREATED` v1; later accepted events = `current+1`; duplicate/stale (`<= current`) return the snapshot without persisting; version gap rejects; `CANCELLED` is terminal; unsupported types / invalid fields throw `TypeError`; `CREATED`/`AMENDED` must leave positive finite `notional` and non-empty `owner`.\n- Defensive-copy all returned states, snapshots, and callback arguments via `structuredClone`.\n\n**Tests added** — Replaced `student-tests.mjs` with 6 `node:test` cases (≥4 required): concurrent progress across trades; duplicate/stale returns snapshot without persisting; version gap / invalid first event reject cleanly; cancelled is terminal; malformed/invalid fields reject with `TypeError`; immutability of returned states/snapshots/callback values.\n\n**Visible test result** — `node --test event-projector.test.mjs student-tests.mjs` → 8 pass, 0 fail.\n\n**Remaining risk** — `structuredClone` cannot clone non-cloneable payloads (functions, etc.); not exercised by the fixture. Stale-version duplicates are silently ignored by design (no separate event-id dedupe). Non-numeric `version` values are compared rather than type-validated."}}
